  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed first-floor wraparound extension, hip-to-gable roof extension and rear dormer would, by reason of their cumulative scale, bulk and design, result in an incongruous and top-heavy form of development. The extensions would appear conspicuous and out of keeping with the prevailing scale, form and character of surrounding dwellings, causing material harm to the character and appearance of the host property and the wider streetscene. Furthermore, the proposed use as a large HMO accommodating up to eight occupants would result in a significant intensification of activity compared with a single-family dwelling. The associated comings and goings of occupants, visitors and vehicles would generate increased noise and disturbance, further eroding the established residential character of this densely built-up area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policies CP5 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5, DMD8, DMD13, DMD14 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the intensification of the property as an 8-bedroom, 8-person large House in Multiple Occupation, together with the associated comings and goings of occupants, visitors and vehicles throughout the day and night, would generate unacceptable levels of noise and general disturbance. The combined impacts would cause significant harm to the living conditions and quiet enjoyment of neighbouring occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Core Policy CP5 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5, DMD8, DMD11 and DMD68 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).",
    "The proposed development, in the absence of a robust parking stress survey and sufficient supporting evidence, fails to demonstrate that the additional parking demand arising from the proposed eight-bedroom, eight-person large House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) could be accommodated within the surrounding highway network without giving rise to unacceptable parking stress, displaced parking, harm to highway safety or disruption to the efficient operation of the local road network. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies T2, T3, T4 and T6 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CP24 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD45 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
